WEBVTT

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/10-0
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:13.657
<v Interviewer>Hello, thank you for making time. I am starting the recording now, and you agreed to this beforehand. The topic is how students plan their time during the semester. Why don't you just tell me what a normal week looks like for you?</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/11-0
00:00:14.077 --> 00:00:38.612
<v Student>Well, um, a normal week is never really normal for me (laughs). I have lectures and seminars on three days, and on the other days I work in a café. So I have to fit the university work in somewhere in between. Every Sunday I write down what is coming up that week. If I don't do that, (...) I usually only notice on Thursday that something is due on Friday.</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/12-0
00:00:38.762 --> 00:00:40.122
<v Interviewer>Mhm.</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/13-0
00:00:40.272 --> 00:00:51.990
<v Student>And then it gets hectic. This semester, for example, I had, um, one term paper and two exams, and they were all in the sa- in the same three weeks.</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/14-0
00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.889
<v Interviewer>And how do you cope when it gets hectic?</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/15-0
00:00:55.309 --> 00:01:15.226
<v Student>I make a kind of emergency plan. (...) I split the tasks into small pieces, two or three a day, and cross them off when they are done. That feels good. Sometimes I don't manage it, though, and then I just sit (inaudible) the whole evening, and the next day I am tired.</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/16-0
00:01:15.646 --> 00:01:19.280
<v Interviewer>Can you tell me an example of how it was in the last exam period?</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/17-0
00:01:19.700 --> 00:02:09.996
<v Student>Yes, sure. In the last exam period my first exam was on a Monday, and I had actually planned everything for the weekend before. Statistics on Saturday, review on Sunday. But then my flatmate had a birthday (laughs), and I only got to bed at three in the morning on Saturday. On Sunday I was, um, pretty unproductive. I sat in front of my notes for hours and hardly kept anything. On Sunday evening I threw my plan away and only looked at the most important topics, the ones that came up often in the exercises. That made me much calmer. And the exam went well, too. Since then I always plan a buffer day, a day when nothing is fixed. That really helps me, because I know there is room when something goes wrong.</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/18-0
00:02:10.416 --> 00:02:17.334
<v Interviewer>It sounds as if the buffer day changed a lot. How about studying in general, do you plan that at fixed times?</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/19-0
00:02:17.754 --> 00:02:38.855
<v Student>No, not at fixed times. I notice that I learn best in the morning, so I put the difficult things in the morning. In the afternoon I do the things that need less concentration, for example sorting literature or answering emails. I have a simple app on my phone for that, but actually I prefer to write on paper.</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/20-0
00:02:39.275 --> 00:02:41.564
<v Interviewer>What do you like better about paper?</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/21-0
00:02:41.984 --> 00:02:54.492
<v Student>I see everything at a glance, and I can cross things off. On the phone something always distracts me. I only look at the calendar for a moment, and ten minutes later I have watched a video (laughs).</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/22-0
00:02:54.912 --> 00:02:58.160
<v Interviewer>What would help you with planning that you do not have at the moment?</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/23-0
00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:19.201
<v Student>I think I am missing an overview of all the deadlines in the semester. Every course names its dates at some point, and they are in five different places. If they were in one place, (...) I could start much earlier. And a hint how long a task really takes, because I almost always estimate it too short.</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/24-0
00:03:19.621 --> 00:03:25.860
<v Interviewer>That was an important point. One last question: What would you advise students in their first semester?</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/25-0
00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:41.192
<v Student>I would say: do not plan every hour, plan the weeks instead. And, um, talk to others about it, because you quickly notice that most people have the same problem. (...) That helped me the most.</v>

7a41d2c8-0b5e-4f93-a6d7-1e8c35f20b94/26-0
00:03:41.612 --> 00:03:46.786
<v Interviewer>Thank you very much, that was very helpful. I am ending the recording now.</v>
